Meta-Harness
A standalone, stdlib-only implementation of "Meta-Harness: End-to-End Optimization of Model
Harnesses" (arXiv 2603.28052).

Portions adapted from google-research/harness2 (Apache-2.0)
https://github.com/google-research/harness2
Copyright 2026 Google LLC. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Adapted code carries a header comment naming its
source file:
- meta_harness/core.py: budget ledger (Ledger, BudgetError), from harness2/core/ledger.py

Designs re-implemented in stdlib Python (designs only, no code copied):
- soketlabs/loop (https://github.com/soketlabs/loop): proposer loop, tool output bounds,
  provider layer, Terminus-style seeds
- rivet-dev/rivet (https://github.com/rivet-dev/rivet): resumable runs, sandbox protocol
- truefoundry/trueforge (https://github.com/truefoundry/trueforge): proposer loop, tool output
  bounds, provider layer, benchmark runner, Terminus-style seeds
- keel (MIT): candidate receipts, crash repair, retries, redaction, read window
